 Simulink.BlockDiagram.createSubsystem - Create subsystem containing specified set of blocks
    This MATLAB function creates a subsystem and moves the specified blocks
    into it.

    Syntax
      Simulink.BlockDiagram.createSubsystem(blocks)
      Simulink.BlockDiagram.createSubsystem()
      Simulink.BlockDiagram.createSubsystem(___,Name,Value)

    Input Arguments
      blocks - Block handles
        numeric array

    Name-Value Arguments
      Name - Name of new subsystem
        character vector | string scalar
      MakeNameUnique - Option to make subsystem name unique
        'on' (default) | 'off'

    Examples
      openExample('simulink/CreateSubsystemFromModelExample')
      openExample('simulink/CreateSubsystemFromModelWithCustomNameExample')

    See also Simulink.BlockDiagram.copyContentsToSubsystem,
      Simulink.BlockDiagram.deleteContents,
      Simulink.SubSystem.convertToModelReference,
      Simulink.SubSystem.copyContentsToBlockDiagram

    Introduced in Simulink in R2009a
